    "result_text": "The test passes. Here's a summary of the full-stack change I made to put an issue date and a due date on each invoice:\n\n**Database** \u2014 `V9__invoice_dates.sql`: a new Flyway migration adding two nullable `issued_date` and `due_date` columns (ISO date literals as `VARCHAR(10)`). Additive, so existing rows and the create path are unaffected.\n\n**Server** \u2014 `Invoice.java`: added `issuedDate`/`dueDate` fields (mapped to the new columns) with getters/setters, so `GET /api/invoices` now serializes both dates on every row. `TestSupportController.java`: extended the `/__test__/seed` insert to persist the fixture's `issuedDate` and `dueDate` via `JdbcTemplate` using the explicit ids.\n\n**Front-end** \u2014 `InvoicesPanel.tsx`: added the two dates to the `Invoice` type, two header cells, and two body cells rendering them under the required `data-testid=\"invoice-issued\"` and `data-testid=\"invoice-due\"` anchors inside each `invoice-row-{id}`.\n\nVerified via `npm run typecheck` (clean) and `bin/e2e` (1 passed). No pinned scaffolding or the spec was touched.",
